course: dictionary
lesson: 12307
title: Big words about big businesses
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Corporate is a word you will meet in the news and on signs. It means to do with a large company or business. «The corporate office is on the tenth floor.» The clue is office: companies have offices, so corporate is about the business, not a school or a home.
explain: Corporate can also mean shared by a whole group. «Corporate responsibility» means that everyone in a company, or any group, has a duty to act fairly. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some people use corporate to mean something that feels businesslike, dull or made only for money. «The party felt very corporate, with stiff speeches and plain grey cups.» The word tells you how the party felt, not what it was made of. This is an informal use, so it can sound negative.
fact: Corporate means to do with a large company or business.
fact: «A corporate logo» is the picture or design a company uses to show who it is.
fact: «Corporate responsibility» means a company treats people and the planet fairly.
fact: Informal use: some people call something bland or dull «corporate», so think about the sentence before you decide.
fact: Phrases to know: corporate event, corporate world, corporate sponsor.
exercise: «The company printed its corporate logo on every bag.» What is a corporate logo? | A loud song | A school lesson | A type of bag | *A company's special picture or design
exercise: «Corporate responsibility means treating people and the planet fairly.» Who does corporate responsibility belong to? | Only the sun | A single person alone | *A whole group, such as a company | Only pets
exercise: Which phrase is about a big business? | Muddy puddle | Bird song | Quiet garden | *Corporate sponsor
test: «The corporate office had a huge glass front.» Where might this office be? | In a field of cows | *Inside a large company's building | On a sandy beach | In a cosy kitchen
test: Sam says the meeting felt corporate, dull and only about money. What does corporate suggest here? | Covered in snow | *Businesslike and dull, made for profit | Full of games and fun | Very loud and funny
exam: Which sentence uses corporate to mean to do with a large business? | «The puppy is asleep on the sofa.» | «We picked apples in the orchard.» | «It rained all afternoon.» | *«The corporate office is on the tenth floor.»
